---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import LessonLayout from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
import LessonHeader from '../../components/LessonHeader.astro';
import LessonNav from '../../components/LessonNav.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import InsightBox from '../../components/InsightBox.astro';
import TagBadge from '../../components/TagBadge.astro';
---

<LessonLayout title="How Compilers Work" lessonNumber="0.1" section="Foundations">

    <LessonHeader lessonNumber="0.1" title="How Compilers Work" description="The 10-minute mental model. After this, you'll understand every step your code goes through to become a running program.">
        <TagBadge variant="concepts">10 min read</TagBadge>
        <TagBadge variant="concepts">No code required</TagBadge>
    </LessonHeader>

    <!-- Section 1: The Analogy -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">A compiler is a translator.</h2>

        <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Think about translating a book from Urdu to English. You'd do it in steps:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
            <div class="step-card bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
                    <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-monk-blueLight flex items-center justify-center">
                        <span class="text-monk-blue font-bold text-sm">1</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold">Read the words</h3>
                </div>
                <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Break text into individual words and punctuation. You don't care about meaning yet — just identifying each piece.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
                    <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-monk-tealLight flex items-center justify-center">
                        <span class="text-monk-teal font-bold text-sm">2</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold">Understand grammar</h3>
                </div>
                <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Figure out which words form sentences. Which is the subject, which is the verb, which modifies what.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
                    <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-monk-greenLight flex items-center justify-center">
                        <span class="text-monk-green font-bold text-sm">3</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold">Check meaning</h3>
                </div>
                <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Does this sentence make sense? Can the subject actually do this action? Are there contradictions?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
                    <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-monk-amberLight flex items-center justify-center">
                        <span class="text-monk-amber font-bold text-sm">4</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold">Write in English</h3>
                </div>
                <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Express the same meaning in the target language. Same ideas, different words.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <InsightBox>
            <p class="text-sm"><strong>That's a compiler.</strong> These four steps, applied to programming languages instead of human languages. Monk source goes in, C source comes out. Same ideas, different syntax.</p>
        </InsightBox>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: The Four Steps -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-6">The four steps, concretely</h2>

        <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">Let's follow a single line of Monk code through the entire compiler:</p>

        <Code code={`let x = 1 + 2 * 3`} lang="javascript" />

        <!-- Step 1: Lexer -->
        <div class="mb-10 mt-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-monk-blueLight flex items-center justify-center">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-blue" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 6.75h16.5M3.75 12h16.5M12 17.25h8.25"/></svg>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Step 1: Lexer</h3>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Read characters, produce tokens</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The lexer reads the source code character by character and groups them into <strong>tokens</strong> — the smallest meaningful units. It's like reading a sentence and identifying each word.</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
                <p class="text-xs text-monk-muted font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Input: raw text</p>
                <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-monk-bg rounded-lg px-4 py-3 mb-4 tracking-wider">
                    l e t &nbsp; x &nbsp; = &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; + &nbsp; 2 &nbsp; * &nbsp; 3
                </div>

                <div class="flex items-center justify-center my-3">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-blue" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"/></svg>
                </div>

                <p class="text-xs text-monk-muted font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Output: tokens</p>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-blueLight text-monk-blue px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-blue-200">LET</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-stone-100 text-stone-600 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-stone-200">IDENT: x</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-amberLight text-monk-amber px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-amber-200">EQUALS</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-greenLight text-monk-green px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-green-200">NUM: 1</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-amberLight text-monk-amber px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-amber-200">PLUS</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-greenLight text-monk-green px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-green-200">NUM: 2</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-amberLight text-monk-amber px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-amber-200">STAR</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-monk-greenLight text-monk-green px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-green-200">NUM: 3</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">The lexer doesn't care about meaning. It just knows <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">let</code> is a keyword, <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">x</code> is a name, <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">1</code> is a number, and <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">+</code> is an operator. Whitespace and comments are discarded.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2: Parser -->
        <div class="mb-10">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-monk-tealLight flex items-center justify-center">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-teal" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 3.75v4.5m0-4.5h4.5m-4.5 0L9 9M3.75 20.25v-4.5m0 4.5h4.5m-4.5 0L9 15M20.25 3.75h-4.5m4.5 0v4.5m0-4.5L15 9m5.25 11.25h-4.5m4.5 0v-4.5m0 4.5L15 15"/></svg>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Step 2: Parser</h3>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Read tokens, produce a tree</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The parser reads the token stream and builds a <strong>tree</strong> that represents the structure of the program. This is called an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).</p>

            <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The critical job: <strong>operator precedence</strong>. The parser knows that <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">2 * 3</code> must be computed before <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">1 + ...</code>. The tree's shape encodes this.</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-6 mb-4">
                <p class="text-xs text-monk-muted font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Output: Abstract Syntax Tree</p>

                <!-- AST diagram using SVG -->
                <svg viewBox="0 0 400 220" class="w-full max-w-md mx-auto" fill="none">
                    <!-- Lines -->
                    <line x1="200" y1="30" x2="100" y2="90" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="200" y1="30" x2="300" y2="90" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="300" y1="90" x2="230" y2="160" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="300" y1="90" x2="300" y2="160" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="300" y1="90" x2="370" y2="160" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="200" y1="30" x2="200" y2="0" stroke="none"/>

                    <!-- Root: VariableDecl -->
                    <rect x="130" y="5" width="140" height="30" rx="8" fill="#FFF4ED" stroke="#E8590C" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="200" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#E8590C" font-size="12" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">VariableDecl "x"</text>

                    <!-- Left: name -->
                    <rect x="50" y="75" width="100" height="30" rx="8" fill="#EFF6FF" stroke="#2563EB" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="100" y="95" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2563EB" font-size="12" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Ident "x"</text>

                    <!-- Right: BinaryExpr + -->
                    <rect x="240" y="75" width="120" height="30" rx="8" fill="#FFFBEB" stroke="#D97706" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="300" y="95" text-anchor="middle" fill="#D97706" font-size="12" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Add (+)</text>

                    <!-- Bottom left: 1 -->
                    <rect x="195" y="150" width="70" height="28" rx="8" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="230" y="168" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16A34A" font-size="12" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Num 1</text>

                    <!-- Bottom mid: Multiply -->
                    <rect x="250" y="140" width="100" height="28" rx="8" fill="#FFFBEB" stroke="#D97706" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="300" y="158" text-anchor="middle" fill="#D97706" font-size="12" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Multiply (*)</text>

                    <!-- Bottom right leaves -->
                    <line x1="275" y1="168" x2="255" y2="200" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <line x1="325" y1="168" x2="345" y2="200" stroke="#E8E4DF" stroke-width="2"/>

                    <rect x="220" y="195" width="70" height="24" rx="6" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="255" y="211" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16A34A" font-size="11" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Num 2</text>

                    <rect x="310" y="195" width="70" height="24" rx="6" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    <text x="345" y="211" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16A34A" font-size="11" font-weight="600" font-family="Inter, sans-serif">Num 3</text>
                </svg>
            </div>

            <InsightBox>
                <p class="text-sm"><strong>Notice the tree shape.</strong> Multiply is nested inside Add, deeper in the tree. When we evaluate bottom-up, <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">2 * 3 = 6</code> happens first, then <code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">1 + 6 = 7</code>. The tree structure IS the precedence.</p>
            </InsightBox>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3: Type Checker -->
        <div class="mb-10">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-monk-greenLight flex items-center justify-center">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-green" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Step 3: Type Checker</h3>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Walk the tree, verify types make sense</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The type checker walks the AST and verifies that every operation is valid. It annotates each node with its type.</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
                <div class="divide-y divide-monk-border">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 px-5 py-3">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-green flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/></svg>
                        <p class="text-sm"><code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">2 * 3</code> — int * int = <strong class="text-monk-teal">int</strong>. Valid.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 px-5 py-3">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-green flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/></svg>
                        <p class="text-sm"><code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">1 + 6</code> — int + int = <strong class="text-monk-teal">int</strong>. Valid.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 px-5 py-3">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-green flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/></svg>
                        <p class="text-sm"><code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">let x = ...</code> — x has no annotation, inferred as <strong class="text-monk-teal">int</strong>. Valid.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm mb-4">Now imagine a mistake:</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-red-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 px-5 py-3">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
                    <div>
                        <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-stone-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">let x int = "hello"</code>
                        <p class="text-sm text-red-600">Error: cannot assign string to int variable</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">The type checker catches this <em>before the program runs</em>. Better to find the bug now than in production.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 4: Code Generator -->
        <div class="mb-10">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-monk-amberLight flex items-center justify-center">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-amber" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17.25 6.75L22.5 12l-5.25 5.25m-10.5 0L1.5 12l5.25-5.25m7.5-3l-4.5 16.5"/></svg>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Step 4: Code Generator</h3>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">Walk the tree, write C</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The code generator walks the type-checked AST and outputs C source code. Each node type has a translation rule.</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-monk-accent font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Monk</p>
                        <Code code={`let x = 1 + 2 * 3`} lang="javascript" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-monk-amber font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Generated C</p>
                        <Code code={`int64_t x = 1 + 2 * 3;`} lang="c" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm mb-4">A more complex example — a function:</p>

            <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-monk-accent font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Monk</p>
                        <Code code={`const add = (a int, b int) int {
    return a + b
}
show(add(3, 4))`} lang="javascript" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-monk-amber font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Generated C</p>
                        <Code code={`int64_t add(int64_t a, int64_t b) {
    return a + b;
}
monk_show(add(3, 4));`} lang="c" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-monk-muted text-sm">The generated C is compiled by your system's C compiler (GCC, Clang) into a native binary. Done.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: The Full Pipeline -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">The complete picture</h2>

        <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">you write</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-monk-accentLight rounded-lg px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-monk-accent">
                        hello.monk
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">lexer</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-monk-blueLight rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm text-monk-blue">
                        Stream of tokens: <span class="font-mono text-xs">LET, IDENT, EQUALS, NUM, ...</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">parser</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-monk-tealLight rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm text-monk-teal">
                        Tree of nodes: <span class="font-mono text-xs">VariableDecl &rarr; BinaryExpr &rarr; ...</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">checker</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-monk-greenLight rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm text-monk-green">
                        Same tree, now every node knows its type
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">codegen</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-monk-amberLight rounded-lg px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-monk-amber">
                        hello.c
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
                    <div class="w-20 flex-shrink-0 text-right">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-monk-muted">cc</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-1 bg-stone-100 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-stone-600">
                        hello <span class="text-monk-muted text-xs">(native binary)</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: What Monk doesn't do -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">What Monk does NOT do</h2>

        <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-muted flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-sm">No bytecode or virtual machine.</p>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-xs">Source goes straight to C. No intermediate bytecode format. No VM to maintain.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-muted flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-sm">No runtime interpreter.</p>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-xs">The output is a standalone native binary. No Monk runtime needed to execute it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-monk-muted flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-sm">No LLVM.</p>
                    <p class="text-monk-muted text-xs">LLVM is a 100+ MB dependency. We generate C instead and let your system's C compiler do the heavy lifting. LLVM can be added later as an optional optimization backend.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6">
            <InsightBox>
                <p class="text-sm"><strong>One exception:</strong> the REPL (<code class="text-xs bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">monk repl</code>) uses a tree-walking interpreter for interactive use. You can't compile and link a binary for every line you type. But compiled output is the primary mode.</p>
            </InsightBox>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: The files you'll write -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">The files you'll write</h2>

        <p class="text-monk-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The Monk compiler is built in Go. Here's what each package does:</p>

        <div class="bg-white border border-monk-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden font-mono text-sm">
            <div class="divide-y divide-monk-border">
