    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Key takeaways</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-monk-accentLight flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                    <span class="text-monk-accent font-bold text-xs">1</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm">A compiler is four steps: <strong>lex</strong> (words), <strong>parse</strong> (grammar), <strong>check</strong> (meaning), <strong>generate</strong> (translate).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-monk-accentLight flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                    <span class="text-monk-accent font-bold text-xs">2</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm">Each step transforms a simpler representation into a richer one. Characters to tokens to trees to typed trees to C code.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-monk-accentLight flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                    <span class="text-monk-accent font-bold text-xs">3</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm">The AST's tree shape encodes operator precedence. Deeper nodes are evaluated first.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-monk-accentLight flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                    <span class="text-monk-accent font-bold text-xs">4</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm">Monk compiles to C, then C compiles to native. No VM, no GC, no runtime.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

